# Create a normal issue (`/iflow-issue`)

`/iflow-issue` authors and creates **one well-specified GitHub issue** (a single deliverable), then optionally sets up the normal lifecycle: branch + `/iflow-init`, then hand off to `/iflow-plan`.

Use it when you want a real issue body (context, spec, acceptance criteria) — not a general-fixes chore bucket and not a multi-issue epic.

This is an **off-path** command — the lifecycle dispatcher (`/iflow`) never auto-runs it, because it creates GitHub issues (and optionally branches). Invoke it explicitly.

## How it relates to other commands

- **`/iflow-pick fix`** — one-shot *general-fixes* issue into `/iflow-plan` → `/iflow-start`. Use `/iflow-issue` when the work is a named, well-specified deliverable.
- **`/iflow-fix`** — iterative small-fixes *session* that stays in a loop until `/iflow-close`. They coexist.
- **`/iflow-epic`** — staged multi-issue work. If the epic **anchor** does not exist yet, create it with `/iflow-issue epic …`, then run `/iflow-epic <N>`.

