## Input

Optional free-form text after the command — a seed for the title and/or short description. Examples:

- `/iflow-issue add dry-run flag to doctor` — seed the draft from that text.
- `/iflow-issue epic Large rewrite` — epic-anchor mode: title prefixed with `Epic:`, apply the `epic` label when it exists.
- `/iflow-issue` — no seed: ask for a one-line intent before drafting.

## Phase 1 — draft and create

1. **Preflight.** Detect the default branch (`gh repo view --json defaultBranchRef -q .defaultBranchRef.name`; fall back to `git symbolic-ref --quiet --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD | sed 's|^origin/||'`, else `main`). Run `git fetch --prune`. Report the current branch and whether the working tree is clean (`git status --porcelain`).

2. **Parse input.** If the first token is `epic` (case-insensitive), enable epic-anchor mode and treat the remainder as the seed. Bare `epic` with no remainder → ask for the epic intent.

3. **Draft title + body.** Propose a title and a body with this light structure (not a full `/iflow-plan`):
   - **Problem / context**
   - **Spec** (what to change)
   - **Acceptance criteria**
   - **Out of scope** (optional; omit the heading when empty)

   Refine with the user until they confirm the text. If the draft is clearly over-large for one PR, **mention** splitting via `/iflow-epic` — do **not** auto-create sub-issues.

4. **Create (confirm first).** Show the final title and body (and, in epic-anchor mode, the planned `epic` label when present). On yes: create with `gh issue create` (add `--repo owner/repo` if ambiguous; add `--label epic` only when epic-anchor mode is on **and** `gh label list` shows `epic`). Capture the returned issue number `N`. Change the chat/agent tab title to `Issue <N> <short title>`. Other labels/milestones: only if the user asked for them in this turn — do not invent them.

## Phase 2 — optional lifecycle setup

5. **Offer branch + init (default path).** Ask whether to start work now. On yes (require a clean tree; if dirty, stop and ask to commit/stash):
   - Build a kebab-case slug from the title; branch name `<N>-<slug>`. Confirm a non-obvious slug.
   - **On the default branch** → `git switch -c <N>-<slug>`.
   - **On a non-default branch** → **ask** whether to branch from the **current** branch or from the **default** branch.
   - Delegate local capture to `/iflow-init` for `<N>` (follow `{{ agent_dir }}/commands/iflow-init.md`). Do not re-implement that logic.
   - **Ask** whether to continue with `/iflow-plan`. Do **not** auto-run it.

6. **Create-only.** If the user declines Phase 2, stop after create. Remind them they can pick it up later with `/iflow-pick` / `/iflow-init`.

## Constraints

- **Off-path:** `/iflow` never auto-dispatches to `/iflow-issue`.
- Never create a GitHub issue or branch without explicit confirmation; show what will be created first.
- GitHub only (`gh`); GitLab is not supported.
- Branch off the detected default (or the current branch when chosen); never force-push or delete branches from this skill.
- Delegate local capture to `/iflow-init`; do not write `issue<N>_plan.md` here.
- Do not merge with `/iflow-fix` or `/iflow-pick fix` — different intents.
